---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<div class="container privacy-page">
		<a href="/" class="home-link">&larr; Home</a>
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<div class="effective-date">
			<span class="label">Effective Date:</span>
			<span>Jan 1, 2025</span>
		</div>
		<p>
			Yantagram ("Yantagram", "we", "us", or "our") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use,
			and protect your information when you use Yantagram, our open-source messaging software. By using Yantagram, you agree to the terms of
			this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, you must not use the Software.
		</p>

		<ul>
			<li>
				<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
				<p>
					Yantagram is designed to operate in a decentralized, peer-to-peer environment and collects minimal personal information by default.
					To improve the Software, we may collect anonymous usage data.
				</p>

				<strong>Anonymous Usage Data</strong>

				<p>We may collect the following information:</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li>Feature usage statistics (e.g., which features are used).</li>
					<li>Performance metrics (e.g., error reports or operation speeds).</li>
					<li>General configuration settings (e.g., operating system and application version).</li>
				</ul>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>2. How We Use the Information</h2>
				<p>We use anonymous usage data to:</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li>Understand user behavior to prioritize future updates.</li>
					<li>Improve Yantagram's performance, stability, and features.</li>
					<li>Identify and address bugs or technical issues.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>3. How We Protect Your Information</h2>
				<p>We take the following measures to protect any data we collect:</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li>Encryption: Any transmitted data is encrypted using industry-standard methods.</li>
					<li>Limited Access: Only authorized personnel have access to collected data.</li>
					<li>Storage: Anonymous usage data is stored securely in a database controlled by Yantagram.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>We do not sell, rent, or share your data with third parties.</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>4. Your Rights</h2>
				<p>
					You have the right to stop using Yantagram at any time. Upon cessation of use, any personal identifying information pertaining to your
					usage will be deleted from Yantagram's systems within three months.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>5. Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest version will always be available on our website. If significant changes
					are made, we will notify you through the Software or our website.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>6. Contact Information</h2>
				<p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at: yantagram@proton.me</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.privacy-page {
		max-width: 800px;
		padding-top: 80px;
		padding-bottom: 80px;
	}

	.home-link {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
		font-weight: 500;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	.home-link:hover {
		color: var(--color-text);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.effective-date {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.effective-date .label {
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-right: 0.25rem;
	}

	p {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	ul {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	li h2 {
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	li p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	strong {
		display: block;
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0.25rem;
	}

	.disc-list {
		list-style: disc;
		padding-left: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.disc-list li {
		margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
	}

	a {
		color: var(--color-primary);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	a:hover {
		opacity: 0.8;
	}
</style>
